--- !u!114 &736840381
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 736840379}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "[Cleaning]\r\n\u201CHe was always early. Not because he had to, just because
    he didn\u2019t like being the last one to explain himself. When he joined the
    force, people laughed. Not strangers. Family friends. People who spoke his language.
    \u2018You?\u2019 they said. \u2018In uniform?\u2019\r\nHe wasn\u2019t trying
    to be a hero, he just wanted to help. The boring kind of good. Showing up. Stepping
    in. Making things quieter, not louder. He didn\u2019t even like the uniform all
    that much. \u2018It makes conversations shorter.\u2019  People stopped talking
    like humans once they saw it. He said it mattered to be seen doing the right
    thing. Maybe it would make the jokes stop.\r\nThat night he was off duty. No
    uniform. No badge out. He saw the cars and ran anyway; because someone needed
    help and he was right there. That\u2019s it. I keep thinking about that part.
    How instinct still overrode fear.\r\nNow everyone wants to argue about procedures,
    about what should have happened. About how fast decisions are made. No one wants
    to talk about how hard he worked to be seen as trustworthy. How careful he was.
    How often he swallowed things just to keep the peace. \u2018It was a mistake.\u2019
    - My ass. That word feels too clean. Like something you wipe up and forget.\r\nHe
    learned this place\u2019s rules better than most people born into them. And still,
    it wasn\u2019t enough. I keep finding myself defending him to strangers. As if
    love needs documentation. He deserved to be met as a person first. That\u2019s
    the part they skipped.\u201D\r\n[Reward]\r\n\u201CThank you for listening to
    his story. He spent his life trying to prove he belonged.\r\nI don\u2019t want
    his grave to have to do the same.\u201D\r\n\r\nMother ; NPC\r\n\r\n\u201CI told
    him not to trust uniforms. Not his. Theirs. He laughed at me. Said I worried
    too much and that things are different now. I have lived long enough to know
    that \u2018different\u2019 is just another way of saying \u2018not for everyone.\u2019\r\nPeople
    from home would laugh like it was a joke. \u2018A cop?\u2019 they\u2019d say.
    \u2018With your face?\u2019  Like it was a costume he had no right to wear. Jokes
    are how people tell the truth without taking responsibility. He wanted to prove
    them wrong. Wanted to show that you can serve a place without erasing where you
    come from.\r\nI go to church more often now. It gives me words when I don\u2019t
    have my own. God sees effort.  He didn\u2019t need that. He believed in action.
    In being \u2018a good man.\u2019 Now I pray differently. Not for answers. Just
    that his name is said correctly. That he is not reduced to an error. Maybe that\u2019s
    why this hurts so much. He did everything they say they want from a good man. 
    And still, they didn\u2019t recognize him.\u201D\r\nI\u2019ll light a candle.
    It\u2019s something I can still do for my son. Even now.\u201D\r\n\r\nShooter
    ; NPC\r\n\u201CTraining tells you to decide fast. Faster than thought. You see
    movement, you see a shape, and your body finishes the sentence before your brain
    does. Told myself I followed procedure.\r\nThen I saw his name. Where he worked.
    How long he\u2019d been on the force. I didn\u2019t see a colleague. I saw a
    threat. That wasn\u2019t instinct. That was learned\u2026 Why did I feel so confident
    in that moment?...\u201D\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
